 "readme": "# SDV MCP Server\n\nThis project provides a local MCP server that wraps the SDV (Synthetic Data Vault)\nworkflow for tabular synthetic data generation, evaluation, and visualization.\nIt also includes a small client script to test the server end-to-end.\n\n## What it does\n\n- **Generate** synthetic tables from local CSV files and metadata.\n- **Evaluate** synthetic data quality against real data.\n- **Visualize** real vs. synthetic distributions for a specific column.\n\nAll operations run locally. No API keys or environment variables are required.\n\n## Project structure\n\n- [mcp_server.py](mcp_server.py): MCP server that exposes SDV tools.\n- [synthetic_ops.py](synthetic_ops.py): Core SDV generate/evaluate/visualize logic.\n- [test_client.py](test_client.py): Client script that runs the server and tests all tools.\n- [dummy_data](dummy_data): Example dataset (CSV + metadata.json).\n- [synthetic_data](synthetic_data): Output folder for generated synthetic CSVs and plots.\n\n## Setup\n\nCreate and activate a Python 3.12 environment, then install the package in editable mode:\n\n```bash\npip install -e .\n```\n\n## Run the MCP server\n\n```bash\npython mcp_server.py\n```\n\nThe server uses stdio transport by default.\n\n## Run the test client\n\n```bash\npython test_client.py\n```\n\nThe test client will:\n\n1. Call `sdv_generate` to create synthetic data in [synthetic_data](synthetic_data)\n2. Call `sdv_evaluate` to print quality metrics\n3. Create a seaborn/matplotlib comparison plot saved to [synthetic_data](synthetic_data)\n\n## Notes\n\n- If you change the dataset folder, update it inside [test_client.py](test_client.py).\n- For visualization, choose a non-ID column (e.g. `rating`).\n",
